<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/graphviz-label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AnnotationTag> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/graphviz-label> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Graph visualization label" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/graphviz-label> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r37765d91d59a5b8b7071428b_nbd1705927a084aaeb650c2eba9e46b5cb1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/graphviz-label> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r37765d91d59a5b8b7071428b_nbd1705927a084aaeb650c2eba9e46b5cb2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/psyinf-ns-id> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This annotation can be used to assign a record identifier within the namespace used by the psychoinformatics project and its knowledge pool. This is useful for three main use cases:\n\n1. A record has a PID in a global namespace, but should also be presented within the psyinf domain (e.g., with a page on the project website). Example: A Person record using an ORCID identifier as the PID.\n2. A record has a random PID, and a human-readable identifier for a URL slug is desirable.\n3. A record has a non-random PID with outdated semantics (e.g., name of the subject changed) and should be presented under a different name." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/psyinf-ns-id> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AnnotationTag> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/psyinf-ns-id> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Psychoinformatics namespace identifier" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/psyinf-ns-id> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r0ebfd727e2c7f81548db3a4d_n90d64ed8fbe149bcafa67990e398a2cdb1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/psyinf-ns-id> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r0ebfd727e2c7f81548db3a4d_n90d64ed8fbe149bcafa67990e398a2cdb2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/psyinf-ns-name> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This annotation can be used to assign a record name within the namespace used by the psychoinformatics project and its knowledge pool. This is useful for two main use cases:\n\n1. A record has a random PID, and a human-readable identifier for a URL slug is desirable.\n2. A record has a non-random PID with outdated semantics (e.g., name of the subject changed) and should be presented under a different name.\n\nThis tag is similar to `psyinf-ns-id`. The difference is that only the last \"path segment\" of the PID is changed (e.g. `persons/<uuid>` would be replaced with `persons/<annotation-value>`)." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/psyinf-ns-name> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AnnotationTag> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/psyinf-ns-name> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Psychoinformatics namespace record name" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/psyinf-ns-name> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r3d53deae5e4076e5a3b296d9_nd18842f401f44ae2b7db292f53447f84b1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/annotation-tags/psyinf-ns-name> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r3d53deae5e4076e5a3b296d9_nd18842f401f44ae2b7db292f53447f84b2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/bibliographic-types/67d65212-cfaf-45a7-819b-6db326dcc817> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A document with blank spaces to be filled in with particulars." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/bibliographic-types/67d65212-cfaf-45a7-819b-6db326dcc817> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZBibliographicType> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/bibliographic-types/67d65212-cfaf-45a7-819b-6db326dcc817> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Form" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/bibliographic-types/67d65212-cfaf-45a7-819b-6db326dcc817> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r9625f1cb40be97e22080648e_nd13d2aecc7684fa4befbf20e92f26033b1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/bibliographic-types/67d65212-cfaf-45a7-819b-6db326dcc817> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r9625f1cb40be97e22080648e_nd13d2aecc7684fa4befbf20e92f26033b2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/16e38ddd-6323-4fc7-abad-398609bf8541> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A formal recognition (title, prize, honor, grant, or certificate) granted to an individual, team, work, or organization on the basis of demonstrated merit, measured by predefined evaluative criteria such as excellence, originality, impact, technical quality, or service—determined through an adjudication process (e.g., jury or peer review). Recipients are selected from candidates submitted via self-nomination or third-party nomination, application, or curated consideration, and selection is documented by the awarding body according to stated eligibility and evaluation procedures." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/16e38ddd-6323-4fc7-abad-398609bf8541> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZCompetitionType> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/16e38ddd-6323-4fc7-abad-398609bf8541> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Merit-based award" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/16e38ddd-6323-4fc7-abad-398609bf8541> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r1ef9bed15104134bcf374d51_n2e15a4c59527462c8f7693ac9bcf8455b1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/16e38ddd-6323-4fc7-abad-398609bf8541> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r1ef9bed15104134bcf374d51_n2e15a4c59527462c8f7693ac9bcf8455b2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/2bbc8baa-108d-4766-8a0c-f69971db192d> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Funding provided by the Initiative and Networking Fund of Helmholtz for projects relating to imaging science." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/2bbc8baa-108d-4766-8a0c-f69971db192d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZCompetitionType> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/2bbc8baa-108d-4766-8a0c-f69971db192d> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broadMatch> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/4e49ac7d-d6da-4131-806b-6425491e26fd> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/2bbc8baa-108d-4766-8a0c-f69971db192d> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Helmholtz Imaging Project Fund" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/49fb3582-cd4c-4fd5-b34e-bb0db771fab8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Collaborative Research Centres are long-term university-based research institutions, established for up to 12 years, in which researchers work together within a multidisciplinary research programme.\n\nThey allow researchers to tackle innovative, challenging, complex and long-term research undertakings through the coordination and concentration of individuals and resources within the applicant universities. They therefore enable institutional priority area development and structural development. Cooperations with non-university research institutions are expressly encouraged.\n\nCollaborative Research Centres consist of a large number of projects. The number and scope of these projects depend on the research programme. Individual projects are led by one researcher or jointly by several researchers.\n " .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/49fb3582-cd4c-4fd5-b34e-bb0db771fab8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZCompetitionType> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/49fb3582-cd4c-4fd5-b34e-bb0db771fab8> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broadMatch> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/4e49ac7d-d6da-4131-806b-6425491e26fd> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/49fb3582-cd4c-4fd5-b34e-bb0db771fab8> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "CRC/TRR" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/4e49ac7d-d6da-4131-806b-6425491e26fd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZCompetitionType> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/4e49ac7d-d6da-4131-806b-6425491e26fd> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Funding programme" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competition-types/4e49ac7d-d6da-4131-806b-6425491e26fd> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r601e5491817ae5d3c0763605_n29cba0eab06d4d3191dfeb8b4ea2504cb1 .
