<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competitions/a34e4534-6181-4f78-a2b5-bf210d8ee235> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/application_deadline> "2026-08-14"^^<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/w3ctr-datetime> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competitions/a34e4534-6181-4f78-a2b5-bf210d8ee235> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r5a0ba498bfa96105c146d5a8_nc73460d18d7043e391790db769e617d6b1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competitions/a34e4534-6181-4f78-a2b5-bf210d8ee235> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r5a0ba498bfa96105c146d5a8_nc73460d18d7043e391790db769e617d6b2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competitions/a34e4534-6181-4f78-a2b5-bf210d8ee235> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/associated_with> _:r5a0ba498bfa96105c146d5a8_nc73460d18d7043e391790db769e617d6b3 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competitions/a34e4534-6181-4f78-a2b5-bf210d8ee235> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/started> _:r5a0ba498bfa96105c146d5a8_nc73460d18d7043e391790db769e617d6b4 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competitions/a34e4534-6181-4f78-a2b5-bf210d8ee235> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "ScienceServe" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competitions/c2a58f79-34f6-49bd-a813-6ac41faf34d9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "KonsortSWD – NFDI4Society is the consortium for the social, behavioral, educational\nand economic sciences within the National Research Data Infrastructure (NFDI). Its goal is\nto support researchers in research data management (RDM) and to establish RDM as an\nintegral part of scientific practice.\nTo achieve this goal, KonsortSWD supports the further development and integration\nof tools for RDM (software, scripts, workflows, portals, etc.), especially for sensitive data,\nas well as the solution of multidisciplinary challenges (multidisciplinary use cases) in\nresearch data management. 1\nWe fund projects that contribute to the improvement, expansion or sustainable use of RDM\ntools, particularly for sensitive data. The submissions are evaluated according to the\nfollowing criteria:\n• Quality of the project, in particular the status of preliminary work (the project builds\non robust preliminary work or already existing mature tools) and connectivity, e.g. to\nservices of KonsortSWD\n• Robustness of the strategy for setting up and operating the project\n• Appropriateness of the schedule and the requested resources\n• Expected long-term added value for researchers in the social, behavioral, educational\nand economic sciences\n• Contribution to the improvement of research data management for sensitive data\nand/or to the solution of multidisciplinary challenges (multidisciplinary use\ncases) in research data management.\nApplications with innovative approaches to supporting RDM (tools, workflows, etc.), e.g. AIbased approaches, are particularly welcome.\nThe call is aimed at:\n• Researchers who wish to develop or further develop methods or software for RDM,\n• Infrastructure providers who wish to complement existing services or introduce new\ncomponents into NFDI consortia." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/competitions/c2a58f79-34f6-49bd-a813-6ac41faf34d9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/topics/research-data-management> .
