<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/0695351c-d792-4208-85a3-2932affeec28> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The I-CHECK-HEART collaborative project is developing an AI-powered app for cardio-oncological follow-up care for cancer patients being treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors. The aim is to detect cardiovascular side effects at an early stage and to better assess individual risk using a data-driven risk score. To achieve this, data from smartwatches, sensors, questionnaires, as well as clinical and laboratory tests, are combined and analysed using machine learning. The resulting risk score is presented using an easy-to-understand traffic-light system, integrated into the electronic health record and guides risk-adapted follow-up care. At the same time, the app enhances patients’ health literacy, self-management and quality of life, whilst relieving pressure on the healthcare system through more efficient follow-up processes." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/0695351c-d792-4208-85a3-2932affeec28> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
