<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/20cb1e21-9518-4d22-bfe3-fe87a1587736> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/started> _:r903440580c3424d7d883a224_na0a9d7b905914df18ca82ed66850f3efb6 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/20cb1e21-9518-4d22-bfe3-fe87a1587736> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "Neuronale Organoide: Wissenschaftstheoretische, ethische und rechtliche Implikationen alternativer, aus Stammzellen gewonnener 3D-Modelle" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/20e67c9d-3754-4079-bd73-a16af0f4b2d9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The research project aims to investigate the organisation of neurochemistry in the brains of humans and macaques by characterising neurotransmitter receptor systems. The focus is on identifying potential evolutionary trade-offs, which are to be discovered using a specific dimensionality reduction technique called ParTI. The aim is to gain insights into neurological and psychiatric disorders and to validate these findings using multimodal imaging, behavioural data and gene expression data, whilst also carrying out interspecies comparisons between humans and macaques to identify evolutionary differences." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/20e67c9d-3754-4079-bd73-a16af0f4b2d9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/20e67c9d-3754-4079-bd73-a16af0f4b2d9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/associated_with> _:r002aa441746e09847f10c422_n3b05ada372814fdfbb8acdd34879efc4b1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/20e67c9d-3754-4079-bd73-a16af0f4b2d9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/ended> _:r002aa441746e09847f10c422_n3b05ada372814fdfbb8acdd34879efc4b2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/20e67c9d-3754-4079-bd73-a16af0f4b2d9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/influenced_by> _:r002aa441746e09847f10c422_n3b05ada372814fdfbb8acdd34879efc4b3 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/20e67c9d-3754-4079-bd73-a16af0f4b2d9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/short_name> "PETParTI" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/20e67c9d-3754-4079-bd73-a16af0f4b2d9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/started> _:r002aa441746e09847f10c422_n3b05ada372814fdfbb8acdd34879efc4b6 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/20e67c9d-3754-4079-bd73-a16af0f4b2d9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "PETParTI - Evolutionary Analysis of Human Neurochemistry" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/236dde03-0176-4747-ad0f-c6346034d05e> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The T‑CARE consortium will reproduce three complementary rodent models of autoimmune limbic encephalitis (ALE) and Rasmussen’s encephalitis (RE) across independent epileptology and neuroimmunology labs, run parallel blinded experiments without and with modified non‑mitogenic/non‑depleting/non‑Fc‑binding anti‑CD3 antibodies (mouse 145‑2C11; rat G4.18), and harmonize SOPs to capture standardized clinical, electrophysiological, imaging, histological and immunophenotyping readouts. By validating model signatures against human ALE/RE tissue and comparing preventive versus therapeutic dosing and routes (i.v., i.n., i.p.), the project seeks to define causal links between T cell–driven antigen presentation, IFN‑γ/STAT1/CCL2‑mediated recruitment of phagocytes, synaptic stripping, neurodegeneration and epileptogenesis, and to identify robust paraclinical biomarkers (exhausted vs regulatory T cell fractions, MRI, EEG, histology) of treatment effect.\n\nTranslationally, the consortium aims to demonstrate that anti‑CD3 immunomodulation induces exhaustion/apoptosis of autoreactive T cells and expands regulatory T cells to reduce immune‑mediated neuronal injury, seizure burden, and the development of chronic focal epilepsy; success will generate a multimodal, FAIR‑aligned preclinical dataset supporting orphan‑designation applications and rapid initiation of clinical proof‑of‑concept trials to repurpose agents such as teplizumab or foralumab for AEAE. Projected outputs include reproducible multicenter preclinical evidence, open‑science dissemination (open‑access publications, society platforms, symposia, patient engagement) and structured pathways for industry and regulatory engagement toward clinical development." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/236dde03-0176-4747-ad0f-c6346034d05e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/236dde03-0176-4747-ad0f-c6346034d05e> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r8e805ba586173eb6706f466e_nf5ee096ef4234cbd8f4f7c653506a0dab1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/236dde03-0176-4747-ad0f-c6346034d05e> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/annotations> _:r8e805ba586173eb6706f466e_nf5ee096ef4234cbd8f4f7c653506a0dab2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/236dde03-0176-4747-ad0f-c6346034d05e> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/associated_with> _:r8e805ba586173eb6706f466e_nf5ee096ef4234cbd8f4f7c653506a0dab3 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/236dde03-0176-4747-ad0f-c6346034d05e> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/short_name> "T-CARE" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/236dde03-0176-4747-ad0f-c6346034d05e> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "Pre-clinical therapy studies for rare diseases using small molecules and biologicals – development and validation" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/2c375332-3be1-4212-934e-a088bbf6fca7> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The ONCOverse project addresses the inadequate and often delayed care provided to patients with pancreatic cancer, an oncological emergency. At its core is the development of a nationwide, interoperable digital platform that systematically records tumour, host and clinical course data and connects stakeholders from the fields of healthcare, research and the patient perspective. By integrating modern diagnostics, wearables, patient reports and AI-based analyses, the aim is to gain a better understanding of individual disease progression and to personalise treatment decisions. ONCOverse also promotes patient-centred involvement, facilitates access to expertise and clinical trials, and supports the implementation of new technologies in an ethical and user-centred manner. The aim is to bring about a paradigm shift towards data-driven, precision medicine-based and comprehensively standardised care for patients with pancreatic cancer." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/2c375332-3be1-4212-934e-a088bbf6fca7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/2c375332-3be1-4212-934e-a088bbf6fca7> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/associated_with> _:r1d46f41e7934a229ea45d2e0_n5887ca697cc64b63a88070bb604abd64b1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/2c375332-3be1-4212-934e-a088bbf6fca7> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/ended> _:r1d46f41e7934a229ea45d2e0_n5887ca697cc64b63a88070bb604abd64b2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/2c375332-3be1-4212-934e-a088bbf6fca7> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/influenced_by> _:r1d46f41e7934a229ea45d2e0_n5887ca697cc64b63a88070bb604abd64b3 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/2c375332-3be1-4212-934e-a088bbf6fca7> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/short_name> "ONCOverse" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/2c375332-3be1-4212-934e-a088bbf6fca7> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/started> _:r1d46f41e7934a229ea45d2e0_n5887ca697cc64b63a88070bb604abd64b6 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/2c375332-3be1-4212-934e-a088bbf6fca7> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "Patient-centric and intuitive evidence generation in Pancreatic Cancer" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/315bb3fe-bfc9-498b-83d3-f655a1eb2f48> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The project aims (1) to investigate the extent to which geometric attributes of brain structures capture individual-level information and (2) to enhance the interpretability of mathematical descriptors, particularly the Laplace-Beltrami operator (LBO) spectrum or LB Shape Descriptor (LBSD), in order to gain novel insights into the brain's geometry and its relation to individual characteristics." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/315bb3fe-bfc9-498b-83d3-f655a1eb2f48> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/315bb3fe-bfc9-498b-83d3-f655a1eb2f48> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/associated_with> _:r66780165979b83197c095a87_n088bb3246325479292d93bce9a59fc96b1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/315bb3fe-bfc9-498b-83d3-f655a1eb2f48> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/ended> _:r66780165979b83197c095a87_n088bb3246325479292d93bce9a59fc96b2 .
