<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/745fed06-c8e7-471b-8cdf-8bd7470e4326> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This project is part of the ExoEnhance project, which investigates biomechanical enhancement – in particular exoskeletons and neuroprostheses – in terms of expected physiological efficacy, subjective bodily experience, social integration and ethical legitimacy. It develops assessment frameworks, design recommendations and ethical guidelines for body-worn assistive and enhancement technologies. " .
