<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/abcd-j> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "Accessing Behavior for Clinical Data and Joint Usage" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/ae2319c1-eb94-455a-8653-5a0d0d7bc68e> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The project investigates how age-dependent modulation of microglial network states influences excitability and connectivity in the thalamocortical system, a key centre for sensorimotor integration in multiple sclerosis (MS). Using animal models, human tissue, co-cultures and large patient datasets, we are analysing immune-glia-neuron interactions at multiple levels. The aim is to identify molecular and network-based signatures that explain MS progression and clinical heterogeneity and pave the way for new therapies." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/ae2319c1-eb94-455a-8653-5a0d0d7bc68e> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> _:r3d3a169b8d6a4d2df5c00bcb_nbd3d1859b91f4a35b11faf224ec2118cb1 .
