<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/ae2319c1-eb94-455a-8653-5a0d0d7bc68e> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "Einfluss einer Modulation des Mikroglia-Netzwerks auf die (Hyper-)Erregbarkeit und Konnektivität des thalamokortikalen Netzwerks" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/b6b7ecc8-c244-46e6-b357-13d15b460bd5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The project \"Normative Molecular Imaging for identifying disease heterogeneity\" (NorMImag) aims to use AI-based normative models to better capture the diversity of disease-specific brain alterations in Alzheimer’s patients. Using FDG-PET data, the models will predict typical brain activity patterns for healthy individuals based on their demographic characteristics, enabling the detection of pathological deviations at the regional level in patients. This approach supports more individualized and automated diagnostics and lays the groundwork for personalized treatment strategies." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/b6b7ecc8-c244-46e6-b357-13d15b460bd5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/b6b7ecc8-c244-46e6-b357-13d15b460bd5> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/associated_with> _:r9ac5bc0a47adcc647882a775_n25e689dac2a443389dd7efebd708dea2b1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/b6b7ecc8-c244-46e6-b357-13d15b460bd5> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/ended> _:r9ac5bc0a47adcc647882a775_n25e689dac2a443389dd7efebd708dea2b2 .
