<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/b6b7ecc8-c244-46e6-b357-13d15b460bd5> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/started> _:r9ac5bc0a47adcc647882a775_n25e689dac2a443389dd7efebd708dea2b6 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/b6b7ecc8-c244-46e6-b357-13d15b460bd5> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "Normative Molecular Imaging for identifying disease heterogeneity" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/ba5fce5c-783a-4e90-be03-392cfe1d06a5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "ExoEnhance investigates biomechanical enhancement – in particular exoskeletons and neuroprostheses – in terms of expected physiological efficacy, subjective bodily experience, social integration and ethical legitimacy. It develops assessment frameworks, design recommendations and ethical guidelines for body-worn assistive and enhancement technologies. Using future scenarios, alongside research in occupational physiology, neurotechnology, the social sciences and ethics, the consortium assesses the opportunities and risks of these enhancement technologies in the context of work and health. Laboratory and field studies investigate the biomechanical effects, efficacy and acceptance factors of various exoskeletons. Qualitative analyses capture experiences of agency and embodiment. Sociological and philosophical sub-projects examine body augmentation as a social phenomenon and develop normative criteria for autonomy and justice. Through participatory formats, practice-oriented guidelines for strategic technology design are developed. The sub-project ‘Exoskeleton Technology Analysis and Integration’ focuses on the practical evaluation of market-ready exoskeletons in laboratory and workshop settings, taking into account the expected diversity of users in the workplace of the future. Future labour market developments suggest a greater diversity of the workforce – in particular, more older workers and people with" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/ba5fce5c-783a-4e90-be03-392cfe1d06a5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/ba5fce5c-783a-4e90-be03-392cfe1d06a5> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/ended> _:r80bc6fb6f0b6fd13ac4237c3_n84fc7f0bf6d5416285d817883b5a15ebb1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/ba5fce5c-783a-4e90-be03-392cfe1d06a5> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/short_name> "ExoEnhance" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/ba5fce5c-783a-4e90-be03-392cfe1d06a5> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/started> _:r80bc6fb6f0b6fd13ac4237c3_n84fc7f0bf6d5416285d817883b5a15ebb2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/ba5fce5c-783a-4e90-be03-392cfe1d06a5> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "Verbundprojekt: Biomechanisches Enhancement und seine gesellschaftliche Einbettung – ExoEnhance" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/c2d2a0d0-a974-46f3-994c-a2699df44b22> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "HELIA is developing a mobile robotic assistance system designed to provide flexible support to healthcare professionals in their day-to-day clinical work. At its core is a no-code approach (EPG system), which enables clinical staff without programming knowledge to create new tasks for a service robot, based on AI models such as vision-language and large-language models. In parallel, the development and testing of the HELIA system are being subjected to a comprehensive ethical, legal and medical analysis, particularly with regard to data protection, transparency and its use with vulnerable patient groups. This analysis takes into account current and future regulatory frameworks such as the GDPR, the AI Act and the European Health Data Space, and links them to practical experience gained from clinical trials. The aim is to develop practical ethical guidelines for the use of AI-supported robotics in medicine and to utilise these scientifically." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/c2d2a0d0-a974-46f3-994c-a2699df44b22> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/c2d2a0d0-a974-46f3-994c-a2699df44b22> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/associated_with> _:ref97bc78f3a9013225b34e8a_n9df8fe34b45e401b9a763859124d61b9b1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/c2d2a0d0-a974-46f3-994c-a2699df44b22> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/ended> _:ref97bc78f3a9013225b34e8a_n9df8fe34b45e401b9a763859124d61b9b2 .
