<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/e2a8b1eb-40b0-4763-9a34-ed864817f00e> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "Distribits 2025" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/e6bca269-1fdc-48c0-9d3a-3d87567e3343> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The NEUROCAST project creates a reference framework for brain development that accounts for diverse brain maturation pathways. It will examine how biological factors as well as environmental conditions and formative life experiences influence individual developmental trajectories. This also involves investigating which patterns are associated with mental resilience or an increased risk of developing mental health conditions. A primary goal is to develop a predictive method that estimates the likely future development of the brain in a single examination. NEUROCAST aims to improve the assessment of risks and disease progression, and enable more personalized treatment based on individual developmental trajectories." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/e6bca269-1fdc-48c0-9d3a-3d87567e3343> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/e6bca269-1fdc-48c0-9d3a-3d87567e3343> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/associated_with> _:r3106151ea6cfe6062b0e4f5e_n5c6d486ec6a1490a9938246b9a823aabb1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/e6bca269-1fdc-48c0-9d3a-3d87567e3343> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/ended> _:r3106151ea6cfe6062b0e4f5e_n5c6d486ec6a1490a9938246b9a823aabb2 .
