<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/e6bca269-1fdc-48c0-9d3a-3d87567e3343> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/short_name> "NEUROCAST" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/e6bca269-1fdc-48c0-9d3a-3d87567e3343> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/started> _:r3106151ea6cfe6062b0e4f5e_n5c6d486ec6a1490a9938246b9a823aabb6 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/e6bca269-1fdc-48c0-9d3a-3d87567e3343> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "Neurodevelopmental forecasting of mental illness in adolescence" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f57f4405-347a-40de-9ab2-8cf60c9124c9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "BRAINTREE investigates the ethical aspects of machine learning-based brain age estimation. Conveniently, the difference between estimated brain age and chronological age – the brain age gap – is generally interpreted as relevant to individuals’ health and as an indicator of disease progression. A growing body of evidence supports the potential utility of brain age for diagnosis, prognosis and as a tool for monitoring treatment. However, there are still significant ethical and interpretative questions that remain unanswered. The BrainTree project aims to systematically address these outstanding questions in order to provide an ethical framework for clinically relevant applications of brain age estimates. The consortium project comprises three work packages, each led by a different partner. Forschungszentrum Jülich acts as coordinator and leads Work Package 3." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f57f4405-347a-40de-9ab2-8cf60c9124c9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f57f4405-347a-40de-9ab2-8cf60c9124c9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/associated_with> _:r0f0d301ad8da784b0cf34f5e_n4902cd9bd66c42a69e0ffc7476e085a2b1 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f57f4405-347a-40de-9ab2-8cf60c9124c9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/ended> _:r0f0d301ad8da784b0cf34f5e_n4902cd9bd66c42a69e0ffc7476e085a2b2 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f57f4405-347a-40de-9ab2-8cf60c9124c9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/influenced_by> _:r0f0d301ad8da784b0cf34f5e_n4902cd9bd66c42a69e0ffc7476e085a2b3 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f57f4405-347a-40de-9ab2-8cf60c9124c9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/short_name> "BRAINTREE" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f57f4405-347a-40de-9ab2-8cf60c9124c9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/started> _:r0f0d301ad8da784b0cf34f5e_n4902cd9bd66c42a69e0ffc7476e085a2b6 .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f57f4405-347a-40de-9ab2-8cf60c9124c9> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/title> "Gehirnalterermittlung- Diagnoseverfahren oder Neukonzeptionierung von Alter – Medizinische und politische Ethik der Brain Age Prediction (BRAINTREE)" .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f81c957f-7042-4983-ac62-eb90a78b747c> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The VINNIE project develops a blended therapy approach for children aged 7 to 12, which combines digital learning resources with a smart therapeutic toy. Via an online platform, the children work alongside a virtual character to learn about their condition and develop coping strategies designed to help them in everyday life. These strategies are transferred to a smart soft toy, which offers practical support in stressful situations and uses biofeedback (e.g. heart rate variability) to visualise learning progress. Supported by neuroethical expertise, the aim is to create effective, practical and potentially transdiagnostic support for psychosomatic, anxiety and obsessive-compulsive disorders." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f81c957f-7042-4983-ac62-eb90a78b747c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/f81c957f-7042-4983-ac62-eb90a78b747c> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/associated_with> _:rd818d15e40c00895a33fccd1_nb5fc3b4f5dee40e5a5bdbbdb54f8cd58b1 .
