<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/trr379> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This project brings together a team of researchers from various German universities to identify transdiagnostic biosignatures of aggressive behavior to enable more specific prevention and treatment. A longitudinal, developmental, multidimensional, transdiagnostic approach is applied to address three primary objectives: 1) transdiagnostic characterization of agression, 2) multilevel mechanistic understanding of biosignatures of aggression, and 3) investigation of the developmental and longitudinal stability of aggression in mental disorders." .
