_:r22f2e47144a14adc8f132f66_n09ea54d9551d441aadd4909c5d87d0dab2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/persons/michael-hanke> .
_:r22f2e47144a14adc8f132f66_n09ea54d9551d441aadd4909c5d87d0dab2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/Attribution> .
_:r22f2e47144a14adc8f132f66_n09ea54d9551d441aadd4909c5d87d0dab3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> .
_:r22f2e47144a14adc8f132f66_n09ea54d9551d441aadd4909c5d87d0dab3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:r22f2e47144a14adc8f132f66_n09ea54d9551d441aadd4909c5d87d0dab3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "We re-used fMRI data taken from the studyforrest-dataset (studyforrest.com) to investigate if BOLD responses of the parahippocampal place area (PPA; Epstein & Kanwisher, 1998, A cortical representation of the local visual environment) correlate with incidential spatial speech cues given by an audio drama's narrator (audio-only variant of the movie \"Forrest Gump\"). Results suggest a standard general linear model (GLM) applied to a complex, auditory stimulus can be used to localize a \"visual area\" in individual subjects." .
_:r22f2e47144a14adc8f132f66_n09ea54d9551d441aadd4909c5d87d0dab4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> .
_:r22f2e47144a14adc8f132f66_n09ea54d9551d441aadd4909c5d87d0dab4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:r22f2e47144a14adc8f132f66_n09ea54d9551d441aadd4909c5d87d0dab4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Is the PPA a visual area? BOLD responses to incidental spatial cues in naturalistic stimulation" .
_:r22f2e47144a14adc8f132f66_n09ea54d9551d441aadd4909c5d87d0dab5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/Proceedings> .
