_:r62a68974124e52d8f9d051e1_n8eaf395b331541c6a0630ce98a11b2beb5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "IXI_VBM-GM-Cat12.8.1_Schaefer-Tian_parcellation" .
_:r62a68974124e52d8f9d051e1_n8eaf395b331541c6a0630ce98a11b2beb6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> .
_:r62a68974124e52d8f9d051e1_n8eaf395b331541c6a0630ce98a11b2beb6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:r62a68974124e52d8f9d051e1_n8eaf395b331541c6a0630ce98a11b2beb6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Cortical and subcortical gray matter parcellations using output from CAT12.8.1. VBM preprocessing (mwp1) of the IXI dataset (see https://brain-development.org/ixi-dataset/) in all available parcellation resolutions using Schaefer cortical (Schaefer et al., 2018) and Tian (Tian et al., 2020) subcortical atlas. Site information is encoded in the subject-ID and therefore not part of the .csv files. Additionally the file collection contains a reduced version of demographics measurements with subjectIDs magic the brain data (SEX_ID (1=m, 2=f) , HEIGHT, WEIGHT, DOB ,  STUDY_DATE, AGE)." .
_:r62a68974124e52d8f9d051e1_n8eaf395b331541c6a0630ce98a11b2beb7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/45e542dd-2d2a-41d0-8399-90f2fde72a21> .
