_:r674bed746d8c47c62314d960_nd5374b755f234af4a87b004e93ff0a93b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Four Notions of Autonomy. Pitfalls of Conceptual Pluralism in Contemporary Debates" .
_:r674bed746d8c47c62314d960_nd5374b755f234af4a87b004e93ff0a93b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> .
_:r674bed746d8c47c62314d960_nd5374b755f234af4a87b004e93ff0a93b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:r674bed746d8c47c62314d960_nd5374b755f234af4a87b004e93ff0a93b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "The concept of autonomy is indispensable in the history of Western thought. At least that’s how it seems to us nowadays. However, the notion has not always had the outstanding significance that we ascribe to it today and its exact meaning has also changed considerably over time. In this paper, we want to shed light on different understandings of autonomy and clearly distinguish them from each other. Our main aim is to contribute to conceptual clarity in (interdisciplinary) discourses and to point out possible pitfalls of conceptual pluralism." .
