_:r97ec38bb50bfa4066924ed74_n7d4ffeedabac4e5e9f67cef06118eba6b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/DOI> .
_:r97ec38bb50bfa4066924ed74_n7d4ffeedabac4e5e9f67cef06118eba6b1 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "10.3389/fnagi.2019.00057" .
_:r97ec38bb50bfa4066924ed74_n7d4ffeedabac4e5e9f67cef06118eba6b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/persons/719c0f2c-1d1b-4d2f-8320-101230f855fa> .
_:r97ec38bb50bfa4066924ed74_n7d4ffeedabac4e5e9f67cef06118eba6b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/Attribution> .
_:r97ec38bb50bfa4066924ed74_n7d4ffeedabac4e5e9f67cef06118eba6b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> .
_:r97ec38bb50bfa4066924ed74_n7d4ffeedabac4e5e9f67cef06118eba6b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:r97ec38bb50bfa4066924ed74_n7d4ffeedabac4e5e9f67cef06118eba6b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "There is an increasing interest in identifying non-invasive biomarkers of disease severityand  prognosis  in  idiopathic  Parkinson’s  disease  (PD).  Dopamine-transporter  SPECT(DAT-SPECT), diffusion tensor imaging (DTI), and structural magnetic resonance imaging(sMRI) provide unique information about the brain’s neurotransmitter and microstructuralproperties.  In  this  study,  we  evaluate  the  relative  and  combined  capability  of  theseimaging modalities to predict symptom severity and clinical progression inde novoPDpatients. To this end, we used MRI, SPECT, and clinical data ofde novodrug-naïvePD  patients  (n=  205,  mean  age  61±10)  and  age-,  sex-matched  healthy  controls(n= 105, mean age 58±12) acquired at baseline. Moreover, we employed clinical dataacquired at 1 year follow-up for PD patients with or withoutL-Dopa treatment in orderto  predict  the  progression  symptoms  severity.  Voxel-based  group  comparisons  andcovariance analyses were applied to characterize baseline disease-related alterations forDAT-SPECT, DTI, and sMRI. Cortical and subcortical alterations inde novoPD patientswere found in all evaluated imaging modalities, in line with previously reported midbrain-striato-cortical network alterations. The combination of these imaging alterations wasreliably  linked  to  clinical  severity  and  disease  progression  at  1  year  follow-up  in  thispatient  population,  providing  evidence  for  the  potential  use  of  these  modalities  asimaging  biomarkers  for  disease  severity  and  prognosis  that  can  be  integrated  intoclinical trials." .
_:r97ec38bb50bfa4066924ed74_n7d4ffeedabac4e5e9f67cef06118eba6b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> .
_:r97ec38bb50bfa4066924ed74_n7d4ffeedabac4e5e9f67cef06118eba6b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:r97ec38bb50bfa4066924ed74_n7d4ffeedabac4e5e9f67cef06118eba6b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "The Combination of DAT-SPECT, Structural and Diffusion MRI Predicts Clinical Progression in Parkinson’s Disease" .
